<h2>Members</h2>

<p>
  <b>GUO Cheng</b> (b.1988 Beijing) is an artist currently living and working in Shanghai. Guo works predominantly in installation, integrating custom software and hardware, mixed media, and spatial intervention. His practice interrogates the material and ideological dimensions of technological systems, examining how infrastructures—from data centers to geological strata—mediate human experience across vastly different temporal scales and constitute complex ecological entanglements. His works employ a composed yet subtly absurdist tone to juxtapose grand temporal and spatial scales with mundane technological artifacts, making visible the often-invisible infrastructures that mediate contemporary life and exploring the symbiotic entanglements at the intersections where ecological and technological spheres overlap.
</p>

<p>
  <b>Weiyi Li</b> (1987,Changsha, China), Weiyi Li obtained a BA from the College
  of Architecture and Urban Planning at Tongji University (2009), an MFA from the
  Yale School of Art (2012), and a PhD from the Royal College of Art (2023). Her practice
  often starts with exploring the fundamental approaches through which humans make
  objects.She contends that when knowledge systems seek to rationalize all human activities,
  tactile experience and embodied information will expose the absurdities of such
  framework.
</p>

<p>
  <b>Dawei Yang</b> (1982, Inner Mongolia, China) is an artist based in Berlin (DE).
  He embarked on his artistic journey by studying art and design at institutions,
  including KHB Weißensee, UdK Berlin, and the China Central Academy of Fine Arts
  in Beijing. Additionally, he worked as a research associate at Burg Giebichenstein
  University of Art and Design in Halle and led interdisciplinary projects such as
  “microbes I – Bacteria Produce Rock.”
</p>

<p>
  <b>Rongkai He</b> (b.1987, Zhuzhou, China) is a designer. He is the founder of graphic
  design practice Atmosphere Office.
</p>

<p>
  <b>Jing He</b> (1984, Kunming, China) is a visual artist and educator lives in Rotterdam（NL）.
  She holds a Master degree from Design Academy Eindhoven (NL), a Bachelor degree
  from Gerrit Rietveld Academie(NL) and a Bachelor degree from Central Academy of
  Fine Art (CN).Jing He’s interest in culture, politics and the history behind various
  daily objects, leads to imaginative visual representations involving various materials
  and mediums.
</p>

